# Mode-Operator Selection

Use **Mode 1** for stable, well-defined problems. Use **Mode 2** (HALIRA) when foundational contradictions or irreducible paradoxes are detected.

**Constraints:** Meta max 2 consecutive; never Non after Meta; Vale use with extreme caution.

Use the **mode-operator-selection** skill for full operator sets per mode, HALIRA step operators, foundational vs manageable contradiction criteria, and state-based adjustments. See `.cursor/skills/mode-operator-selection/SKILL.md`.
